.\" Manual page for computo.
.\" Generated wording matches computo --help; keep the two in step.
.TH COMPUTO 1 "2026-10-12" "Computo 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
computo \- JSON data transformation engine (script execution and REPL)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B computo
\fB\-\-script\fR \fISCRIPT\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIINPUT_FILES\fR...]
.br
.B computo
\fB\-\-repl\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIINPUT_FILES\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B computo
is the unified CLI for the Computo engine, a safe, sandboxed, thread\-safe
JSON\-native data transformation language with a Lisp\-like syntax expressed in
JSON. Scripts can be written in either
.B JSON syntax
(the native format) or
.B sugar syntax
(a human\-friendly alternative with infix operators, arrow lambdas, and path
access); the CLI auto\-detects the format and can convert between the two.
.SH MODES
.TP
.BR \-\-script " " \fIfile\fR
Execute the script from \fIfile\fR (auto\-detects JSON or sugar syntax).
.TP
.BR \-\-repl
Start the interactive REPL.
.SH CONVERSION
.TP
.BR \-\-tocomputo " " \fIfile\fR
Convert a JSON script to sugar syntax (.computo).
.TP
.BR \-\-tojson " " \fIfile\fR
Convert a sugar syntax (.computo) script to JSON.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-comments
Enable JSON comment parsing.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debugging features (REPL only).
.TP
.BR \-\-array =\fIkey\fR
Use a custom array wrapper key (default: "array").
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " \fIfile\fR
Reformat the script with semantic indentation.
.TP
.BR \-\-highlight " " \fIfile\fR
Display the script with syntax highlighting.
.TP
.B \-\-color
Force colored output (with \-\-highlight).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output (with \-\-highlight).
.TP
.B \-\-list\-operators
Output a JSON array of all available operators.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Show the help message.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Show version information.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
computo \-\-script transform.json data.json
computo \-\-script script.computo data.json
computo \-\-tocomputo transform.json
computo \-\-tojson script.computo
computo \-\-script transform.json data.json \-\-array="@data"
computo \-\-repl \-\-comments users.json orders.json
computo \-\-repl \-\-debug
computo \-\-format script.json
computo \-\-highlight script.computo
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The full language reference and the libcomputo API documentation live in the
project README and at the Computo documentation site (see the repository
HarryPehkonen/Computo).
